<title>USA: Genovese Drugs may be buyout target - Bizweek.</title>
<headline>Genovese Drugs may be buyout target - Bizweek.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Drug retailer Genovese Drug Stores could be the next buyout target in the consolidating drug industry, Business Week magazine reported.</p>
<p>Analyst Mike Kicera of the New York-based MRK Capital Management was quoted in the September 16 issue of Business Week as saying that a possible buyer would be J.C. Penny Co, which owns the $1.9 billion Thrift Drug Stores and recently bought the 272-store Fay's drug chain.</p>
</text>
